json.dump({"prediction":pred,"rationale":"I matched the parcel's prepared (smoothed, standardized) band series with a short matching window (m up to 24, chosen as the longest with R<=0.1, giving R=0.034), which leaves 30 historical blocks as candidate donors instead of the 4 a long window would leave. Simplex weights (non-negative, summing to one) fitted on the latent standardized series keep the observed scale and avoid extrapolation; greedy forward selection kept two blocks (the most recent, weight 0.81, and one from three years earlier, weight 0.19), so the forecast blends the parcel's recent seasonal trajectory with an earlier analogous segment. Equal band weighting and prediction from observed forward values keep all three bands on their natural scale."},open("answer.json","w"),indent=1)
print(len(pred),"visits written")
EOF

